# Snap Sites WP

Snap Sites WP is a WordPress Multisite plugin that lets network super admins spin up polished, editable starter websites for customers. It includes a template picker UI, site creation flow, shared starter-page structure, and placeholder licensing hooks for future plan enforcement.

## Features

- Multisite-ready site creation via WordPress APIs
- Template cards for Local Business and seven Pro templates
- Per-template setup functions
- Shared starter styling and reusable component classes
- AJAX-based site creation and JSON responses
- Site list for monitoring created sites
- Plan-limit logic structure for future licensing
- Fully editable starter content via normal WordPress pages and menus

## Included templates

- Local Business (Free)
- Corporate (Pro)
- Hotel (Pro)
- Fashion (Pro)
- Real Estate (Pro)
- Beauty (Pro)
- Restaurant (Pro)
- Clinic (Pro)

## Installation

1. Upload the plugin folder or copy the plugin files into `wp-content/plugins/snap-sites-wp/`.
2. Activate the plugin in the WordPress admin.
3. Ensure the site is running in a WordPress Multisite network.
4. Open the network admin menu item `Snap Sites`.

## Usage

1. Open `Snap Sites` from the network admin.
2. Choose a template card.
3. Enter optional site details if needed.
4. Click `Create Site`.
5. The AJAX flow creates the site, creates pages, menu, and starter content, and returns the site URL, admin URL, username, and password.

## Template architecture

The plugin keeps separate setup functions for each template, for example:

- `ssw_setup_local_business_template()`
- `ssw_setup_corporate_template()`
- `ssw_setup_hotel_template()`
- `ssw_setup_fashion_template()`
- `ssw_setup_real_estate_template()`
- `ssw_setup_beauty_template()`
- `ssw_setup_restaurant_template()`
- `ssw_setup_clinic_template()`

These functions create the pages and starter content for each site while preserving a shared component system.

## Security

- Network admin-only capability checks
- Multisite validation
- AJAX nonce checks
- Sanitized and escaped output
- `switch_to_blog()` / `restore_current_blog()` usage when creating site content
- Graceful JSON errors

## Future licensing hooks

The plugin includes a function stub:

```php
ssw_user_can_access_template( string $template_id, string $plan = '' ): bool
```

This currently allows the network super admin to access all templates for testing and can be extended to enforce plan/license-based template access later.

## Notes

- This is intentionally a starter implementation designed for easy extension.
- Image placeholders are handled with layout blocks and neutral placeholders rather than random hotlinked images.
- The design is intentionally polished but broad enough to be edited by a customer without custom design work.

